# finds the node typed as >= 2 primordial domain classes beyond ClassDeclaration and returns >= 1 row.
# The fixed product/frame.ttl (a ontology:Class, model:ClassDeclaration, model:Product — ClassDeclaration
# + ONE structural kind) is the conformant counterpart in the base data graph.
#
# Depth-gate compliance: the subject is NOT typed owl:Class or owl:NamedIndividual (so no 200-char
# comment / specific-type obligation), only the primordial model: domain classes that make it a
# V1ClassDeclarationPunShape focus — exactly the shape of the forbidden pun.

@prefix model: <urn:silmaril:primordial:type:> .

# --- a ClassDeclaration punned into two domain classes (INVALID: model:Product AND model:Frame) ---
<urn:silmaril:fixture:algebra:v1:classpun:negative>
